space_Veins smoke tests. Please ignore.

To run this simulation, execute the script `sim/space_veins_testsims/space_veins_test/runall`.

This simulation requires sumo-launchd to be started and listening for
connections on a TCP socket, e.g. using "~/lib/veins/src/veins/bin/veins_launchd -vv".

This test checks that calculations of the elevation angle are correct and that only packets from satellites above the minimum elevation angle are received.

Setup:
- 1 satellite at an elevation angle of 25.00905°
- 1 satellite at an elevation angle of 24.98552°
- 1 satellite at an elevation angle of 15.00272°
- 1 satellite at an elevation angle of 14.97598°
- 1 satellite at an elevation angle of  -0.0286°

- 1 run with minElevationAngle = 15°
- 1 run with minElevationAngle = 25°

Functionality:
- vehicles and satellites send UdpBasicApp packets to each other
- received packets are counted and compared to the expected value



